{# ── Hero stage ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   The motion is not a boxed illustration beside a text column: it is the
   hero's full field, and the copy sits on it.

   THE FILM IS OURS. It is authored in tools/hero-film from this site's own
   tokens, typefaces and layout language and rendered at build time, so the
   subject is a business presence being formed — intent, identity, digital
   surfaces, readiness — and not a licensed architectural scene that read as a
   property campaign.

   Desktop LTR locales use the right-composed poster and the same full-size
   project sequence, with matching opening/closing frames. RTL keeps its
   approved originals. Portrait phones retain the approved mobile cut.
   Media is never mirrored: embedded words retain their original direction.

   Poster-first by construction: the <source> elements carry data-src, not src,
   so a <video autoplay> with no resolvable source downloads NOTHING until JS
   decides motion is both permitted (not reduced-motion, not Save-Data) and
   needed (near the viewport, tab visible). Reduced motion, Save-Data and no-JS
   therefore cost zero video bytes rather than "load, then stop".

   The approved studio poster is also the film's first and last frame, so the
   resting state, first paint and finished state stay continuous. The film does
   NOT loop: it plays once and returns to the poster, and the control becomes a
   replay.

   The poster <img> carries intrinsic width/height inside a sized stage, so
   there is no black frame, no blank frame and no layout shift. The video sits
   on top at opacity 0 and is revealed only once it is genuinely playing, and
   it is inset by 1px so the poster stays strictly the larger element and
   therefore always wins LCP. Do not remove that inset without re-measuring. #}
<div class="hero-stage" data-hero-motion aria-hidden="true">
  <picture class="hero-stage-poster">
    {% if loc.dir == "ltr" %}<source media="(min-width:1001px)"
            srcset="/assets/motion/zohar-hero-poster-desktop-ltr.svg" type="image/svg+xml">{% endif %}
    <source media="(max-width:860px) and (orientation:portrait)"
            srcset="/assets/motion/zohar-hero-master-mobile.webp" type="image/webp">
    <img src="/assets/motion/zohar-hero-master-desktop.webp" alt=""
         width="1280" height="720" decoding="async" fetchpriority="high">
  </picture>

  <video class="hero-stage-video" autoplay muted playsinline preload="none"
         disablepictureinpicture disableremoteplayback tabindex="-1">
    <source media="(max-width:860px) and (orientation:portrait)"
            data-src="/assets/motion/zohar-hero-master-mobile.webm" type="video/webm">
    {% if loc.dir == "ltr" %}<source media="(min-width:1001px)" data-src="/assets/motion/zohar-hero-master-desktop-ltr.webm" type="video/webm">{% endif %}
    <source data-src="/assets/motion/zohar-hero-master-desktop.webm" type="video/webm">
    <source media="(max-width:860px) and (orientation:portrait)"
            data-src="/assets/motion/zohar-hero-master-mobile.mp4" type="video/mp4">
    {% if loc.dir == "ltr" %}<source media="(min-width:1001px)" data-src="/assets/motion/zohar-hero-master-desktop-ltr.mp4" type="video/mp4">{% endif %}
    <source data-src="/assets/motion/zohar-hero-master-desktop.mp4" type="video/mp4">
  </video>

  {# Desktop captures are composed responsively outside the copy column.
     The video remains the playback clock; fitting the original captures here
     avoids baking a viewport-dependent crop or a text collision into a film.
     Images load only when desktop motion is permitted and requested. #}
  <div class="hero-projects" data-hero-projects>
    <div class="hero-projects-stage">
      {% for project in ["sadafronia", "better-world", "eco-tech-israel", "zohar-crm", "yayin", "le-monde-sefarade"] %}
      <img data-project-src="/assets/work/{{ project }}-card@2x.webp"
           alt="" width="1600" height="1000" decoding="async">
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>

  {# Two scrims: one along the copy edge for contrast, one at the foot so the
     stage resolves into the page instead of ending on a hard line. #}
  <span class="hero-scrim-edge"></span>
  <span class="hero-scrim-foot"></span>
</div>
